# Naming Conventions

## General Naming Principles

- **Language**: All names MUST be in English
- **Format**: Use snake_case (elements separated by one underscore)
- **Meaningful**: Names should be meaningful, distinct, and pronounceable
- **Clarity**: Make variables and columns/tables clear from their name
- **Avoid misleading**: Do not use names which could misguide data users

---

## Data Lake Terms

| Term | Text Format | Snake Case Format |
|------|-------------|-------------------|
| Data lake | datalake | datalake |
| Data lake layer | datalake layer | datalake_layer |
| Layers | raw, clean, enrich | raw, clean, enrich |

