## Database Column Naming Conventions

### Data Lake Columns

| Source Column Type | Convention | Examples |
|-------------------|------------|----------|
| id (table) | `id` | `id` (house) |
| Foreign key | `id_{foreign_key_property}` | `usuario_id` → `id_user` |
| Name property | `{property}_name` | `nome` (user) → `user_name` |
| Timestamp | `ts_{property_in_past_tense}` | `created_at` → `ts_created` |
| Date | `dt_{property_in_past_tense}` | `dataAssinado` → `dt_signed` |
| Epoch (unix) | `epoch_{property_in_past_tense}` | `event_unix_timestamp` → `epoch_event` |
| Boolean | `is_{property}` or `has_{property}` | `temImovel` → `has_house`<br>`ativo` → `is_active` |
| Modified column | `mod_{clean_col_name}` | `is_penthouse_mod` → `mod_is_penthouse` |

